## ABDM Sandbox Integration and Exit Process

The Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission has developed building blocks and APIs to offer a seamless digital healthcare experience for all stakeholders – health facilities, patients and healthcare workers. The digital infrastructure developed is now accessible to health facilities and health tech players for integration.

This section offers step-by-step guidance on the following for interested stakeholders:

- Guidelines to integrate ABDM-powered services (ABHA Number capture & verification, HIP services, HIU application) in the testing environment called Sandbox
- More details are provided in the given document
- Process to exit sandbox and deploy application in facilities located across all States and UTs.

Kindly note that the functional requirements and process steps are intended for the ABDM integrations across all States and UTs.

### A. End-state Patient experience

Integrations with ABDM infrastructure can be leveraged to achieve the following patient experience:

We recommend developing this experience in three milestones, each building over the previous:

- Milestone 1: ABHA Number creation and capture & verification for seamless patient registration. excel
- Milestone 2: Building Health Information Provider (HIP) services to share digital records via Personal Health Records (ABHA) app. excel
- Milestone 3: Developing Health Information User (HIU) services to provide view of patient’s medical history to authorized healthcare workers with complete consent

Guidance on milestone-wise functional requirements has been shared in Section C. Sandbox exit requirements & process has been detailed in Section D.

### B. Getting started – Sandbox registration

The first step to integrate with ABDM ecosystem is to register on Sandbox – kindly fill out a short form providing details about your organization and your motivation to join.

Post internal approval, you will receive credentials to access ABDM APIs. Kindly expect a revert by the Sandbox support team within a timeline of 3-4 days post application.

### C. Milestone-wise functional requirements

Before you begin with integrations in Sandbox environment, kindly ensure you have the client bridge ID and secret to access ABDM APIs. Please refer to Section B to understand the registration process.

Also, please refer to the functional test cases in Section D (Step 1) to understand mandatory/optional workflow features.

For any technical concerns regarding integration, kindly post query on the devforum.

#### C.1  ABHA Number creation and capture & verification

The steps involved and recommended workflow are as follows:

- Register partnering facility (HIP) in ABDM Sandbox Health Facility Registry
- Collaborate with HIP staff to provide patients with information regarding ABHA Number and ways to create one on their ownPatients with a smartphone can download ABDM Health Records app/any other ABHA Mobile Application to register their ABHA Number. Suggested collateral you can install in facilities to promote ABHA Number benefits can be found in link (English version and Hindi version)Those without a mobile phone can avail assistance at facility registration desk to create an ID using Aadhaar biometric Kindly leverage the existing ABDM Assisted ABHA Number creation portal and consider distributing registration cards with ABHA Number QR code for future capture
