## HIP Initiated Linking

### HIP Initiated Linking 1.0

HIP initiated linking is a process where the HIP can link the patient’s care context with the ABHA Number when the HIP has finished the patient registration and has uploaded the health records in their system

To achieve this the HIPs need to do the following:

- Get user auth for the action they want to perform. There are two different modes of Authentication -Mediated (Mobile OTP, Aadhaar OTP, User Demographics)Direct1. LINK - for purpose of adding care-contexts subsequently. User details are not returned in this case.2. KYC - for getting basic user details.3. KYC_AND_LINK - for requesting user details
- Using the "linking token" returned above for linking, HIP can subsequently add care-contexts in subsequent API call /links/link/add-contexts.

The following sections describe the flows to be built by HIP.

### 1. HIP Initiated Linking For The Patients With Mobile Number

The hospital registers the patient and typically uploads patient records in HIP’s EMR/EHR systems. The hospital will ask the patient if they wish to link the hospital record with their ABHA Number. The hospital will then send the request to CM with the patient preferred authentication mode and the ABHA Number. If the patient preferred authentication mode is OTP based, then the patient will receive an OTP which is forwarded to the CM. The CM validates the OTP and creates a new access token just for the purpose of linking. This new access token is passed to the HIP. The HIP has to call the CM with the new access token to add the care contexts.

HIP initiated linking with authentication type as mobile OTP

### 2. HIP Initiated Linking For The Patients With Demographic Details

If the patient preferred authentication mode is user demographic based, then the patient will have to share their name, YOB, gender which is forwarded to the CM. The CM validates the user details and creates a new access token just for the purpose of linking. This new access token is passed to the HIP. The HIP has to call the CM with the new access token to add the care contexts.

HIP initiated linking with authentication type as user demographics

### 3. HIP Initiated Linking For The Patients With DIRECT Auth

In case of Direct authentication mode, HIP initiates the request with authMode DIRECT. This request gets added to the list of authorization requests on the consent manager which can be approved by the user. Once the user approves the direct authorization request, CM creates a new perpetual access token for the purpose of linking. This new access token is passed to the HIP. The HIP has to call the CM with the new access token to add the care contexts.

HIP initiated linking with authentication type as DIRECT

### HIP Initiated Linking 2.0

#### 1. Overview Of The Functionality

HIP Initiated linking is the process through which an HIP links the patient’s care context (health record) with the patient ABHA Address, after patient registration and creation of health records (in their HMIS/LMIS system).

Care context (Health record) linking happens in two steps

- Link token generation
- Linking care context with ABHA address after obtaining valid link token

#### 2. Link Token Generation

To achieve linking, the HIPs need to have a valid link token. There are two possible ways to get the link token

- Through scan and share profile use case
- Using link token service

The link token will be used for linking multiple number of care contexts, and concurrent linkages.

