## Overview

Health Facilities can participate in assisted issue of ABHA Numbers to their patients. In this document we outline a technical approach that can be adopted by HIMS / LIMS software to integrate the process easily into their software. The process involves

- Addition of a button to their HIMS / LIMS registration page.
- Clicking the button results in a new window being launched. This window loads the ABHA Number creation page.
- Assisted creation can be performed via Aadhaar or other KYC documents. Aadhaar is simple and the ABHA Number software supports any Aadhaar registered biometric fingerprint device to be used.
- The operator can enter the Aadhaar number and capture the biometric of the user. The system will perform an e-KYC and also determine if this user has been issued an ABHA Number earlier.
- If there is an existing ABHA Number the same is re-used, otherwise the system creates a new ABHA Number for the user.
- It is recommended that for users without mobile phones, a printed version of the ABHA Number card be handed over to the patient for further use.
- The ABHA Number details created (or found) are posted to the HIMS system via the share profile API.
- This allows for the HIMS / LIMS to not only to rapidly issue a ABHA Number but also capture the same information as part their patient registration.

### Technical Pre-requisites For HIP/HMIS Login

- The partnering facility (HIP) must register on the Health Facility Registry
- Ensure that the Bridge ID provided by the partner HRP is registered in the Health Facility Registry (Register HIP section) to enable transfer of profiles across the gateway.

### ABHA Number Creation Through Facility Share Profile

The steps involved and recommended workflow are as follows:

- The partnering HRP must register on the ABDM Sandbox.
- The HRP should implement a button/link on the patient registration form to trigger the ABHA Number creation by calling the URLin a modal window.requestId Param is a unique number for this request (Optional).customCode is HIP internal code to identify target kiosk window. After successful creation of the ABHA Number using the modal window through ABHA Number portal, Callback API will be called by gateway passing the same custom Code So that HRP can populate the profile information in patient registration screen.

