## Getting Started With APIs

### Authenticating With Gateway

Each health repository obtains a time-limited token, valid for X number of seconds, with which it identifies itself to the Gateway. When the token's time limit elapses, the health repository should call sessions API to renew the token. When calling any API, the health repository should pass the authentication token as part of the 'Authorization' http header. In order to obtain the authentication token, the health repository can call /sessions API along with the clientId and ClientSecret they have received.

```
curl --location --request POST 'https://dev.abdm.gov.in/gateway/v0.5/sessions' --header 'Content-Type: application/json' --data-raw '{
  "clientId": "clientId-you-received",
  "clientSecret": "secret-you-received"
}'
```

The above would respond with response like

```
{
    "accessToken": "Some-JWT-Access-Token",
    "expiresIn": 300,
    "refreshExpiresIn": 1800,
    "refreshToken": "Some-JWT-Refresh-Token",
    "tokenType": "bearer"
}
```

Once you have the above response, then for any API call, you must add the "accessToken" as "Authorization" header for the API call. Remember to append "Bearer " before the token

### Updating Your Health Repository URL

When you have received communication from ABDM Sandbox team about setup of your Health Repository, we would have configured your setup with your system URL that you had mentioned in the request email. Its quite possible that your system URL changes over time, and to assist you there is a specific "Dev Service" which you can call to update your system URL. In future, we plan to extend the "Dev Service" with various self servicing APIs. To update your system URL do the following:

- Authenticate with Gateway as above
- Call 'dev service' API with requried information

```
curl --location --request PATCH 'https://dev.abdm.gov.in/devservice/v1/bridges' --header 'Content-Type: application/json' --header 'Authorization: Bearer your-access-token-from-gateway-session' --data-raw '{
	"url": "https://my-hrp-url.com"
}'
```

### Register The Facility That Your Repository Services

To start receiving calls from the Gateway to your Health Repository system, (e.g. patient looking to link records), you need to register the HIP and HIU servies that your Repository services.

- Register the HIP or HIU Service using the following API

```
