## Opt Out Of ABDM

ABDM has facilitated provisions to enable a user to opt out of the ABDM ecosystem, if they wish to do so.

A user can opt out of the ABDM ecosystem in one of the following ways:

- - Delete ABHA Number: A user can permanently delete their ABHA Number.
- - Deactivate ABHA Number: A user can temporarily delete their ABHA Number, and reactivate it at a later stage.

As entities including HIP/HRP/HIU/HL may have health data of a user linked with their ABHA Number in their systems, they will have to adhere to few responsibilities to ensure that the user intended action is complete.

When a user deletes/deactivates/reactivates their ABHA Number, the ABDM Consent Manager will send a notification to all the HIP/HRP/HIU/HL linked with the ABHA Number.

On receipt of the notification, the following action must be taken:

Delete ABHA Number

HIP/HRP
- On receipt of the notification, the HIP must unlink the deleted ABHA Number from any health data associated with the user in their system.
- The HIP must acknowledge the notification with a confirmation that the ABHA Number has been unlinked within 7 days of receipt of the notification. Failure in compliance may lead to a penalty.
- The HIP must not generate or link health records for the user with the deleted ABHA Number.HIU
- On receipt of the notification, the HIU must unlink the deleted ABHA Number from any health data associated with the user in their systemHL
- Health lockers are directed to permanently disable login/authentication through the deleted ABHA Number.
- Health lockers are advised to allow access to a user with methods of authentication other than ABHA Number.

Deactivate ABHA Number

HIP/HRP
- On receipt of the notification, the HIP must unlink the deactivated ABHA Number from any health data associated with the user in their system.
- The HIP must not generate or link health records for the user with the deactivated ABHA Number for the period of deactivation.HIU
- On receipt of the notification, the HIU must unlink the deleted ABHA Number from any health data associated with the user in their system.
- HIU must not send any consent requests for viewing/accessing health data to the deactivated user.HL
- Health lockers are directed to temporarily disable login/authentication through ABHA Number.
- Health lockers are advised to allow access to a user with methods of authentication other than ABHA Number.
- Health lockers will be able to deactivate subscription request

Reactivate ABHA Number

HIP/HRPOn receipt of the notification, the HIP must resume linking health data to the reactivated ABHA Number.HIUOn receipt of the notification, the HIU must resume sending consent requests for viewing health dataHLHealth lockers are directed to re-enable login/authentication through ABHA Number.


