## Feb 2022 - New Capabilities For Health Repository Providers & ABHA Apps

Read this note if you are an EMR / LMIS / ABHA software provider who is integrating your software with the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission.

Summary Of New Capabilities

- New APIs for HRPs to declare and register health facilities that use their software.
- Modified API for HRPs to notify ABDM when there is a new health record.
- Revised Test cases for HRPs to get production access.
- Enhanced Provider search APIs for ABHA Apps

The new APIs and Swagger documentation is live on the ABDM Sandbox. All integrators are expected to first ensure their systems work correctly on sandbox before migrating to production.

HRPs Can Now Declare Facilities That Use Their Software

ABDM will support 2 methods to onboard health facilities

- Facility declared process – In this process, the health facility is expected to sign up on the Health Facility Registry and then link the ABDM compatible HRP software it plans to use.
- HRP declared process – This is a new process where the HRP can declare the presence of the health facility in the Health Facility registry (HFR) via an API. The HRP can then link their software with the Facility ID obtained from the declaration. The Health Facility Registry will display such facilities as “Declared by HRP Name”. A nodal contact from the HRP will be linked to the declared facility in HFR. The nodal person can transfer control of the declared facility to the actual facility manager whenever they decide to take control of their record on the Health Facility Registry.

This process is expected to be used by any EMR/LMIS provider to declare the facilities that use their software. Every HRP gets a set of production Client ID / Client Secrets that maps to only ONE endpoint URL in the ABDM registry. Multiple HIPs (health facilities) can be linked to this single end point. If you require multiple end points to be registered in ABDM for your HRP, please write to integration.support@nha.gov.in

All APIs provided in the document are for the ABDM Sandbox. Remove the letters “sbx” for the production URLs

Step 1: Register The Nodal Contact For The HRP

- Create Healthcare Professional ID (HPR ID) of nodal contact – You need to generate a Healthcare Professional Id (HPR ID) using your Aadhaar on https://hpridsbx.abdm.gov.in/register?origin=HFR . Please create your HPR ID as a Facility Manager. Once the 14 digit ID is generated, please set a password as well.
- Once you have the HPR ID and the password is set, head to the swagger page of HPR Id https://hpridsbx.abdm.gov.in/api/swagger-ui.html#/. Expand the “Authentication” tab and select “/v1/auth/authPassword” API. Please fill in the request body and execute this API. Save the “token” returned in the response as it will be used in the header of HFR’s create API.

