### Revised Test Cases For HRPs To Get Production Access

NHA has updated the set of test cases for Milestones M1 and M2 that HRPs are expected to comply with as on Feb 9th 2022. These test cases can be downloaded from https://sandbox.abdm.gov.in/docs/integration and_exit_process.

The key improvements to note are

- HRPs must notify ABDM if there is any new health record created in their system via the patients/sms/notify2 API even if a ABHA address was not collected during registration.
- HRPs must correctly Implement the Discovery and Linking APIs. During discovery, ABDM passes verified IDs to the HRPs. They must search first for any of the verified IDs – first ABHA address and if that is not found Mobile No. If any records match, then they must perform a fuzzy match to verify the name is phonetically similar, ensure age is +/- 2 years and gender is an exact match. This will required to ensure that a patient who is searching for their records will find it.
- On linking of any care context by the user post discovery, the HRP must save the ABHA address in their system against the user. All new records for the same user must be linked using the HIP initiated linking process.
- HRPs must implement the Heart Beat API.

