## HIP Initiated linking 2.0 (Beta)

API HIP Initiated linking 2.0 (Beta)

## Overview Of The Functionality

HIP Initiated linking is the process through which an HIP links the patient’s care context (health record) with the patient ABHA Address, after patient registration and creation of health records (in their HMIS/LMIS system).

Care Context (Health Record) Linking Happens In Two Steps

- Link token generation
- Linking care context with ABHA address after obtaining valid link token

#### 2. Link Token Generation

To achieve linking, the HIPs need to have a valid link token. There are two possible ways to get the link token

- Through scan and share profile use case
- Using link token service

The link token will be used for linking multiple number of care contexts, and concurrent linkages.

#### 3. Link Token Generation API Sequence

The figure below is the sequence diagram for link token generation

#### 4. API Information Request Response

4.1 Link-Token-Generation

This API endpoint will be used to generate linking token by HIP/HRP

