## Consent Management 2.0 (Beta)

## Overview Of The Functionality

The service used to handle consent management before sharing the health data between the entities (HIP, HIU, PHIU)

There are a couple of essential attributes required for consent artefact like, Purpose, HI Types, Access mode, Requester, Range and Validity.

The Consent management can be classified into two types

- 1. Explicit Consent
- 2. Implicit Consent

Explicit Consent: This will be initiated by the HIU (Hospital, Doctor) for accessing the patient health data Implicit Consent: This will be automatically initiated when the user/patient discovery and share his own health data

HIE-CM will validate HIU request for authenticity, replay attack, timestamp, ABHA address, etc.… The request will be saved into the consent_request table in the database The consent request id will return to the called HIU for future tracking purpose The valid requests will be broadcasted to priority queue and send to all the ABDM compliance Patient HIU (PHR application)

The consent notification status will be saved into the consent_notification Upon successful acknowledgement the consent artifact will be generated and saved into consent_artefact HIECM will further share this consent artefact with HIP and HIU.

