## Identity Provider Service 2.0 (Beta)

## Overview Of The Functionality

IDP service authenticates user/patient using two methods one using demographic details another is using ABHA number, ABHA address via mobile OTP

User/patient authentication via demographic details:Demographic details: name, gender, year of birth. In this case we need to search the details from the identity database and the record found then we will return status as TRUE or FALSE and preferred ABHA address to the user

User/patient authentication using ABHA number, ABHA address via mobile OTP:The service should identify the user/patient using ABHA number, ABHA address etc. This service searches the details from the identity database and send the OTP to mobile number and email address [if exist] using the ABDM notification service

Upon successful verification ABDM system shall return the preferred ABHA address and KYC information [name, gender, date of birth, mobile number]

