### Q46. What if patient does not share any ABHA Address with the health facility?

If the patient visiting the health facility (onboarded on ABDM eco-system) does not have any ABHA address or number. Patient can then proceed to register by providing Name, DoB, Gender and Mobile. Patient may then proceed to get treatment and generation of health records. Health facility then notifies HIE-CM of a new health record for mobile number of the patient. No other details are shared, i.e, no details of health record type or patient demographic details are shared. On this mobile number, simply SMS is delivered informing visit of the patient to the health facility. This workflow is explained in detail on webpage, https://sandbox.abdm.gov.in/docs/deep_linking_phr For additional details, may please refer section#5, 'Share Patient profile with HIP' on webpage https://sandbox.abdm.gov.in/docs/build_hip

