### Q49. How FHIR and SNOMED CT linked?

Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) is a standard describing data formats and elements and an application programming interface (API) for exchanging electronic health records. While SNOMED CT is a systematically organized computer-processable collection of clinical terminologies providing codes, terms, synonyms, and definitions. SNOMED CT can be used while recording the clinical details of individuals in electronic records. In FHIR, many elements in resources have a coded value, where SNOMED CT terminology can be referred to document clinical content in a standardized format and to achieve semantic interoperability.

